      "id": "q1",
      "type": "multiple-choice",
      "difficulty": "knowledge-check",
      "stem": "The graph of $y = x^3$ passes through which of these points?",
      "options": [
        {
          "id": "a",
          "text": "$(2, 6)$"
        },
        {
          "id": "b",
          "text": "$(-1, 1)$"
        },
        {
          "id": "c",
          "text": "$(2, 8)$"
        },
        {
          "id": "d",
          "text": "$(-2, 4)$"
        }
      ],
      "correctAnswer": "c",
      "explanation": "When $x = 2$: $y = 2^3 = 8$, so $(2, 8)$ lies on the curve. Note that $(-1)^3 = -1$ not $1$, and $(-2)^3 = -8$ not $4$."
    }
  ]
